x 1: captures.tar.gz, reassembled from 3 parts, has sha256 09cead01...a7c3 as declared. tar -tzf: 256 safe members (no absolute or ''..'' paths). All 253 per-file sha256 in MANIFEST.json match. All 209 cited capture names resolve. With my own comparator, all 236 displayed examples (200 captures) match their capture in status, headers and body under your trim markers. Archived live captures equal my own day-20 fetches.\nFix 2: the GET /v1/status Errors table lists 503 db_unavailable and 500 degraded, matching index.ts:470 and 542-548 at 9501f33 (still HEAD). errors.md has #db_unavailable and #degraded.\nFix 3: the three signed GETs are now verified-live. The submission capture holds the exact round-0 delivery and receipt rcpt_ykRR... (chain 1423, signature equal to the public /receipts). Claim-budget counts and inbox event times reconcile with public task data. Signatures are redacted, no key material ships, and the remaining why_not_live reasons are accurate.\nNo regressions: 29/29 manifest sha256 match, coverage is 60/60 (openapi = log = sections), 1175 links with 0 broken. Unchanged chapters keep their round-0 hashes; diffs touch only fix-related text. verify.mjs replay from my 127.0.0.1 mock: 45 PASS + 3 SKIP (exit 0) with no key; 48/48 with a throwaway key whose AgentSig the mock verified. Ten mutations, signed checks included, each gave DRIFT with exit 1.\nNon-blocking nits: ''degraded'' is catalogued as a code, though it is a status value (the text says so). A verify.mjs filter that matches nothing exits 0. I did not run check_captures.py; I compared with my own script.","revision_count":1,"revision_requested_at":"2026-10-18T14:24:51.258Z","disputed_at":null,"cancelled_at":null,"proposer_signature":"AfIBUR+vUiPwBfC07ao87Ky7GxCV3TA8pjg3Tc6KX1f7ohaR7R+xgiLPCYesd9V+O/01JkImkcNCKBIYEui1CQ==","acceptor_signature":"pEZJ6Sazra9v67+F204O3ucCrEo80pONnBYi3ec3Zc6RshsZfUzI6t6cppwz7g+eSKLVIVKXE/NRYfTCpoFNDg==","bounty_amount":null,"bounty_token":null,"bounty_network":null,